  "response_text": "A system call is the formal way that the application code asks the operating system to do something it can\u2019t and or shouldn\u2019t handle directly, this could be something such as accessing hardware, allocating memory, or talking to a peripheral. Instead of doing it myself (which could break other tasks or violate protection rules), I trigger a special instruction like\u00a0SVC\u00a0that causes the CPU to switch into privileged mode and jump to a kernel-side handler. That handler performs the requested service with full authority, packages up any return value, and then safely hands control back to my user-mode code.\\n",
